---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Driftstack"
  description="iPhone Safari sessions, on demand. Premium fidelity for the device that matters. $2.99 trial pack — 16 hours, no subscription required."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-24 pt-20 md:pt-28">
      <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            iPhone Safari sessions, on demand
          </p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-5xl">
            Premium fidelity for the device that matters.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-lg text-slate-600">
            Driftstack runs real iPhone Safari, on Apple silicon, billed by the
            browser-hour. No emulation. No fingerprint compromises. The same
            fidelity the device delivers, callable from your code.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
            <a href="/pricing#trial-pack" class="btn-primary">Get started — $2.99 trial pack</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-gui/releases" class="btn-secondary"
              >Download GUI client</a
            >
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">
            16 hours of iPhone Safari sessions · no subscription required · use within 14 days · one-time
            purchase, used once per account.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
            <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300"></span>
            <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300"></span>
            <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300"></span>
            <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-500"
              >driftstack-typescript-sdk</span
            >
          </div>
          <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-xs leading-6 text-slate-800"><code>{`import { Driftstack } from '@driftstack/sdk';

const ds = new Driftstack({ apiKey: process.env.DRIFTSTACK_API_KEY });

const session = await ds.sessions.create({
  archetype: 'iphone-16-pro-ios-26',
});

await session.navigate({ url: 'https://example.com' });
await session.interact({ tap: '#cta' });
const state = await session.getState();

await session.destroy();`}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Driftstack -->
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">Real device</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">No emulation tax</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-slate-600">
            Driftstack runs WebKit on real Apple silicon, not a chromium fork
            with a user-agent swap. The fingerprint, layout quirks, and
            JavaScript engine all match the device because they are the
            device.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            Browser-hour metering
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Pay for what runs</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-slate-600">
            Sessions meter by the browser-hour, not by call count. Read 50 elements,
            navigate 20 pages, take 100 screenshots — same hour, same line item.
            Concurrency caps are hard limits at session creation; nothing else
            counts against you.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">EU stack</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">GDPR by default</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-slate-600">
            Compute on Hetzner Falkenstein. Data on Neon EU + Upstash EU +
            Cloudflare R2 EU. Sub-processor list locked and listed in the DPA.
            US-residency questions answered without footnotes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing teaser -->
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">Pricing</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            Start with a $2.99 trial pack.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-slate-600">
            16 hours of iPhone Safari sessions to evaluate, then a tier that
            fits the workload — from $29/mo Starter to custom Enterprise. One
            transparent price ladder, no bait-and-switch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/pricing" class="btn-primary">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Self-hosted teaser -->
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">Self-hosted</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            Run Driftstack on your own Apple silicon.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-slate-600">
            For teams with privacy requirements, high-volume workloads, or
            full data-sovereignty needs. Bring your own Mac Mini M4 (Solo),
            Mac Studio M4 Max (Pro), or Mac Studio Ultra / Mac Pro / multi-node
            cluster (Enterprise). GA within 6 months of API public launch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900">When self-hosted makes sense</h3>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-oxblood-700">→</span>
              <span>Privacy-required workloads where session content must not leave your perimeter.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-oxblood-700">→</span>
              <span>Sustained &gt;5,000 browser-hours per month where unit economics favour owned hardware.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-oxblood-700">→</span>
              <span>Full data sovereignty over recordings, screenshots, and request artefacts.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/self-hosted" class="btn-secondary mt-6">Contact sales</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
